{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1228178-repurposing-vampires-and-starspawn","id":1228178,"title":"Repurposing Vampires and Starspawn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-17T18:46:56-07:00","id":1228178,"title":"Repurposing Vampires and Starspawn","content":"A friend of mine and I were spitballing ideas for a new chronicle and began talking about two things we both love. Vampires and Cthulhu. This is when he had an interesting idea. Replace the vampire of an ALTERNATE WOD with starspawn like entities. It did not make much sense to me at first, then we started drinking and started talking. A mutation, passed along by bite, turning you into a Starspawn-inspired monster with a knack for ancient blood magic. <br /> <br /> Most of the rules would stay the same. Weakness to sunlight, torpor, feeding, reproduction etc...just with lovecraftian inserts. <br /> Blush of life might need a bit of houseruling...but appearing as an actual tentacled monster would increase the importance of ghouls and possible cults. <br /> I wasnt a huge fan of the idea in the beginning but blood magic, dealing with losing your humanity, and being a monster of the night (the stars (sun) are not right) kind of makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> Then I started thinking about how I could adapt each clan into a differant strain of Spawn. <br /> <br /> What does the community at large think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T19:11:52-07:00","id":1228185,"title":"","content":"If possible, read <i>The Rhesus Chart</i> and <i>The Nightmare Stacks</i> by Charles Stross. That setting is very Mythos-like, and those books deal with <s>Vampires</s> (There is no such thing as Vampires).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T04:04:54-07:00","id":1228248,"title":"","content":"I don't really see what this adds that isn't already present. I feel like it just dials the subtly back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T04:43:52-07:00","id":1228253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1228178-repurposing-vampires-and-starspawn#post1228178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine and I were spitballing ideas for a new chronicle and began talking about two things we both love. Vampires and Cthulhu. This is when he had an interesting idea. Replace the vampire of an ALTERNATE WOD with starspawn like entities. It did not make much sense to me at first, then we started drinking and started talking. A mutation, passed along by bite, turning you into a Starspawn-inspired monster with a knack for ancient blood magic. <br /> <br /> Most of the rules would stay the same. Weakness to sunlight, torpor, feeding, reproduction etc...just with lovecraftian inserts. <br /> Blush of life might need a bit of houseruling...but appearing as an actual tentacled monster would increase the importance of ghouls and possible cults. <br /> I wasnt a huge fan of the idea in the beginning but blood magic, dealing with losing your humanity, and being a monster of the night (the stars (sun) are not right) kind of makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> Then I started thinking about how I could adapt each clan into a differant strain of Spawn. <br /> <br /> What does the community at large think?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T21:39:34-07:00","id":1228499,"title":"","content":"The idea behind this adaptation came from a conversation about why WoD was so...well dark. Why is this incarnation of the world not only saturated by the worst of humanity but scores of supernatural horrors?<br /> <br /> One answer? The contagion. The contagion is a parasite embedded deep within the world of darkness, a discarded shell pulled around an abomination. From this spreading corruption comes all manner of monster and malady. An aberration with it\u2019s tentacles so deep in our reality that no god...or machine could pull it out without bringing the whole house of cards down. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s embedded in the heart of a sick world and bound up in the gears of the very occult matrices that are responsible for reality. <br /> <br /> What does this nameless undergod want? Who is to know. It is vast and we are tiny. Even angels can only guess and hack away at it in futility. <br /> <br /> In it\u2019s wake monsters spawn from darkened recesses, spirits clamor through weakening walls, and the human heart is tempted to ever greater acts of depravity. <br /> <br /> Monsters have no mother, but a great uncaring father too massive, alien, and self absorbed to even know they are being born in legion. <br /> <br /> Who are some of these monsters? <br /> <br /> The Progeny. Creatures of once living flesh now...something else. Wretches clinging to the tattered cloaks of their humanity hiding from a sun that no longer recognizes them. Heirs to ancient blood magic and predators among men and beast. <br /> <br /> 5 clans of abberants, each with its own approach to the requiem. Tentacled faces surrounding lamprey maws. Temporary guises of humanity hide these victims of circumstance, but not for long. <br /> <br /> Hipsters blurt \u201cCthulhu ftaghn\u201d but Lovecraft would shrink away in shame and horror if he knew what really lurked in the dark. <br /> <br /> In this splintered world the Progeny take up chorus in the dirge. A requiem for a world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T01:07:49-07:00","id":1228800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1228178-repurposing-vampires-and-starspawn#post1228178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine and I were spitballing ideas for a new chronicle and began talking about two things we both love. Vampires and Cthulhu. This is when he had an interesting idea. Replace the vampire of an ALTERNATE WOD with starspawn like entities. It did not make much sense to me at first, then we started drinking and started talking. A mutation, passed along by bite, turning you into a Starspawn-inspired monster with a knack for ancient blood magic.<br /> <br /> Most of the rules would stay the same. Weakness to sunlight, torpor, feeding, reproduction etc...just with lovecraftian inserts.<br /> Blush of life might need a bit of houseruling...but appearing as an actual tentacled monster would increase the importance of ghouls and possible cults.<br /> I wasnt a huge fan of the idea in the beginning but blood magic, dealing with losing your humanity, and being a monster of the night (the stars (sun) are not right) kind of makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> Then I started thinking about how I could adapt each clan into a differant strain of Spawn.<br /> <br /> What does the community at large think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I for one am a big fan of HP Lovecraft's work and even more the mythos it has inspired.<br /> <br /> My homebrew includes many a nod, and in particular the Rebalancing I've done to Mage completely inserts Lovecraft themes from both the Cthulhu Mythos and Dreamlands.<br /> If you care how I do that for Mage see these Spoilers:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The following has some additional benefits besides the Lovecraft favor, it gives a solid in-world reason for powerful Mage to organize their less potent counterparts into action when concerning the Abyss, thus leading to compelling reasons for adventures. It keeps certain class of foes frightening to even the most powerful Mages and thus prevents them from running amok, and three it flattens the expected power level of whom they can expect to meet within the Material World making the world not a mere playground of Giant and Gods that dwarf the PCs, and increases the need for leaning on social organizations and thus engage in political game play if the PC gain significant Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Three simple tweaks is all it takes:<ul><li>Using Mana Spent on spell casting add to the minimum Paradox roll instead of allowing Mana to mitigate Paradox dice (More powerful effects require mana making more powerful spells carry a risk of uncontrolled magic and paradox conditions. (The in world metaphysics I justify it thusly: Mana, the raw energy of pure Supernal Truth and thus is a potent force of change, but expending it while spellcasting leaves a hole where that Truth was and because spellcasting already has cracks that allow the Abyss to seep in, the vacuum left behind by the spell's consumption of the Mana in that situation creates an active draw for the Abyss and route for it to travel.</li> <li><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">Every dot of Gnosis comes with a Ban which universally apply to Mages of that Gnosis or higher, and the Bans interlock creating increasingly severe limitations on interacting with the Abyss and eventually the Lie as they gain more profound understanding of Supernal Truths and thus Supernal Power. (As per the following chart example from the document for my Homebrew which I am current editing)</span></div></li> </ul><div align=\"center\"> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Gnosis </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"46\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Trait Max </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"71\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Yantras </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"84\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Paradox for over Reaching</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Bans</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>1 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"46\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>5 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"71\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>2 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"84\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>1 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Can't affect Conditions, or Tilts of the Personal, Persistent, and/or Environmental types with the Abyssal tag with Supernal Magic.</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"