tyle=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>2 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Can't </b></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>affect physical beings with the Abyssal tag with Supernal Magic.</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>4 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"46\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>5 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"71\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>3 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"84\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>2 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith, Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Can't anything which have the Abyssal tag with any supernatural ability.</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>5 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"46\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>5 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"71\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>4 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"84\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>3 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>All supernatural effect under your control immediately ends when within sensory range of a being or entity with the Abyssal tag.</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>6 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"46\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>6 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"71\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>4 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"84\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>3 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith, Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Can't remain in the Material World unless in a location with an Ascendant Condition which matches your Paradigm Bane.</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>7 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"46\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>7 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"71\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>5 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"84\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>4 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith, Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Can't remain in the Material World unless in a location with an Open Ascendant Condition which matches your Paradigm Bane. </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>8 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"46\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>8 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"71\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>5 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"84\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>4 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith, Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Can't remain in the Material World unless in a location with an active Gateway Manifestation which relies on an Open Ascendant Condition of Paradigm which matches your Paradigm Bane. </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>9 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"46\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>9 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"71\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>6 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"84\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>5 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>All supernatural effects under your control immediately end when the effect enters the Material World.</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>10 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"46\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>10 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"71\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>6 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"84\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>5 </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> <td width=\"370\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Can't perceive the Material World or anything in it (even yourself), because you literally cannot experience the grossest aspects of the Lie (though that doesn\u2019t prevent them from affecting or even killing you).</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:Lilith, Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:LLNRV U+ Futura T, Futura T, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Pulled into nearest otherworldly Iris when their required Condition or the Condition chain below collapses. Mages without the Paradigm Bane with this level of Gnosis are always pulled into nearest otherworldly Iris if they find themselves in the Material World, which they can</span></span></span></span></span></span>not enter.</span><ul><li>Making timely resolving Paradox Condition more important so the Mage is likelier to face the consequences of their use of Magic by making Paradox Conditions have two stages and not able to be scoured until they have set in and never simply fade away, like so</li> </ul><div align=\"left\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>My Paradox Condition Rewrite</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Paradox Conditions </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">Paradox Conditions can only be gained in one of the following ways \u2014 obtaining a dramatic failure when casting a spell after incurring a Paradox, netting an exceptional success on a released Paradox roll, or failing to fully contain a Paradox. Each one has two resolution mechanics. The first requires the character to actively accept the negative consequence of the Paradox, and the other is to allow the Paradox to lapse. A Paradox Condition lapses after an amount of time determined by the character\u2019s Wisdom if she does not take action to resolve the Condition. Until the Condition is resolved or lapses and have been Scoured, the mage cannot use magic to mitigate the effects of the Paradox. </span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Wisdom </b></span></td> <td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Duration of Paradox Condition </b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">Enlightened </span></td> <td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">One Story/Month </span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">Understanding </span></td> <td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">One Chapter/Day </span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">Falling </span></td> <td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">One Scene </span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">Mad One </span></td> <td width=\"134\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 7px\"><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">One Turn </span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">If the Paradox Condition is allowed to lapse, the Abyss enters the mage\u2019s Pattern, appearing in her Nimbus and the mage exchange the Paradox Condition for a Persistent version of the Condition which no longer may be resolved except by being Scoured, though it\u2019s previous resolution clause now becomes a clause as a source of Arcane Beats, and also causes every spell she casts is tainted by the Abyss and gains a Paradox die even if she does not attempt to Reach as part of the spell. These Conditions are normally referred to as a \u201cStain\u201d to quickly differentiate it from the version which may be resolved without Scouring. At this point, the only way for the mage to remove the taint reflected Persistent Paradox Condition is to Scour it out, similar to Pattern Scouring for Mana as described on p. 87. Removing the taint caused by the failure to resolve a Paradox Condition after it lapses in this manner deals a single point of Resistant lethal damage to the mage, but she does not gain Mana from the Scouring. This Scouring does grant an Arcane Beat, as per normal Paradox Condition Resolution, but does not work until the duration where it could be resolved normally has Lapsed.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The following example Paradox Conditions are not exhaus*tive. The Storyteller is encouraged to invent his own.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Abyssal Nimbus</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This Condition has the Abyssal Tag. The mage\u2019s Nimbus is disfigured by the Abyss, the corruption cascading through her sympathetic links. The mage, and any subjects affected by her Nimbus (including sympathetic ties influ*enced by her Long-Term Nimbus, anyone affected by her Nimbus Tilt, and anything imprinted with her Signature Nimbus), gain the Resonant Condition applicable to Abyssal entities. If the Paradox roll that inflicted this Condition rolled an exceptional success, she gains the Open Condition instead.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">In addition, the Abyssal corruption is readily apparent to any*one who scrutinizes her Signature Nimbus, and her Long-Term Nimbus effects become twisted by the unreality of the Abyss. A Moros\u2019 Long-Term Nimbus might cause bizarre materials with impossible atomic properties to appear, while the religious reve*lations of an Obrimos\u2019 Nimbus take on a nihilistic tone.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Resolution: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">An Abyssal Entity uses the Condition to Manifest.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Nimbus Stain [Persistent]</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This Condition has the Abyssal Tag. The Nimbus disfiguration by the Abyss has seemed in deep, and the corruption is still cascading through her sympathetic links. The mage, and any subjects affected by her Nimbus (including sympathetic ties influenced by her Long-Term Nimbus, anyone affected by her Nimbus Tilt, and anything imprinted with her Signature Nimbus), gain the Base Ephemeral Entity Condition applicable to all types Ephemeral Entities with the Abyssal Tag. If the Paradox roll that inflicted this Condition rolled an exceptional success, she gains the Open Condition instead.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">In addition, the Abyssal corruption is readily apparent to anyone who scrutinizes her Signature Nimbus, and her Long-Term Nimbus effects become twisted by the unreality of the Abyss. A Moros\u2019 Long-Term Nimbus might cause bizarre materials with impossible atomic properties to appear, while the religious reve*lations of an Obrimos\u2019 Nimbus take on a nihilistic tone.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">Finally, every spell she casts is tainted by the Abyss and gains a Paradox die even if she does not attempt to Reach as part of the spell. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Resolution: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">The mage Scours their Pattern as if to gain Mana, but instead of gaining Mana they instead cleanse this Condition from their Pattern, thus resolving it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Arcane Beat:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"> An Abyssal Entity uses the Condition to Manifest</span><br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Imago</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">This Condition has the Abyssal Tag. The Abyss has warped the mage\u2019s ability to clearly envision her Supernal will. Whenever the mage casts a spell, she </span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><i>must </i></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">spend additional Reach equal to the successes earned on the Paradox roll that inflicted this condition. If she does not, the spell automatically fails and adds dice equal to the caster\u2019s spellcasting dice pool to the Paradox roll.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Resolution: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">The mage successfully casts a spell that does not risk more than Paradox Chance Die, the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern, or the mage allows the Condition to lapse after the specified time. </span><br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Imago Stain [Persistent]</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">This Condition has the Abyssal Tag. The Abyss has warped the mage\u2019s ability to clearly envision her Supernal will. Whenever the mage casts a spell, she </span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><i>must </i></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">spend additional Reach equal to the successes earned on the Paradox roll that inflicted this condition. If she does not, the spell automatically fails and adds dice equal to the caster\u2019s spellcasting dice pool to the Paradox roll.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">Finally, every spell she casts is tainted by the Abyss and gains a Paradox die even if she does not attempt to Reach as part of the spell. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Resolution: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">The mage Scours their Pattern as if to gain Mana, but instead of gaining Mana they instead cleanse this Condition from their Pattern, thus resolving it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Arcane Beat:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"> The mage successfully casts a spell that does not risk more than Paradox Chance Die.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Backlash</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This Condition has the Abyssal Tag. The mage has drawn the attention of a vast Abyssal intelli*gence called an Annunaki, which seeks to corrupt the mage\u2019s spells further. The next time the mage casts a spell that risks Paradox, add dice to the Paradox pool equal to the number of successes earned on the Paradox roll that inflicted this condition.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Resolution: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">The mage fully contains a Paradox</span><br /> <b>Abyssal Backlash Stain [Persistent]</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This Condition has the Abyssal Tag. The mage has drawn the attention of a vast Abyssal intelli*gence called an Annunaki, which seeks to corrupt the mage\u2019s spells further. The next time the mage casts a spell that risks Paradox, add dice to the Paradox pool equal to the number of successes earned on the Paradox roll that inflicted this condition.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">Finally, every spell she casts is tainted by the Abyss and gains a Paradox die even if she does not attempt to Reach as part of the spell. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Resolution: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">The mage Scours their Pattern as if to gain Mana, but instead of gaining Mana they instead cleanse this Condition from their Pattern, thus resolving it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\"><b>Arcane Beat: </b> The mage fully contains a Paradox</span></div> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:MS Reference Sans Serif, sans-serif\">For vampires the Humanity and Detachment mechanics are beautiful allusion to the Shadow over Innsmouth as they slowly lose that which made them human. Also replace the dark mother and pagan imagery from Circle of the Crone and instead have it be a far greater fractured competing cults to various Old Ones, and have Longitus be one of the Masks of </span>Nyarlathotep (the Lance already have a few rituals that are Egyptian themed, alluding to the Black Pharaoh) and pull from <a href=\"http://www.lovecraft-stories.com/story/herbert-west-reanimator\" target=\"_blank\">Herbert West -Reanimator</a>, <a href=\"http://www.lovecraft-stories.com/story/beyond-the-wall-of-sleep\" target=\"_blank\">Beyond the Walls of Sleep</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.lovecraft-stories.com/story/from-beyond\" target=\"_blank\">From Beyond</a> for the Ordo Dracul and you are well on your way.</div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-20-2018, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T13:42:23-07:00","id":1228952,"title":"","content":"A lot of the rules stay the same, or have a minor modification. It is mostly fluff I will adapt as I go. <br /> <br /> One rule that will need working with is Blush Of Life. the rule originally makes a vampire look alive, but the new blush of life mechanic will make the progeny look like the human they were before they were changed.<br /> <br /> Ventrue and Daeva spend one vitae To appear as the human they used to be until the next sunrise.<br /> Mekhet and Gangrel spend a vitae to look human for an hour or spend an additional will power point to look human for the rest of the night. <br /> Nosphoros (nosferatu) only have the option to spend a vitae to look somewhat human for an hour. They do not look healthy. They appear as a normal vampire would without the blush of life. pale, Unhealthy, and they must make a conscious effort to blink and breathe. <br /> <br /> Regardless of clan all progeny return to their True form When entering day sleep or falling into torpor. When they do sleep they do not appear dead but as hibernating aberrations. For this reason securing a haven is key, And a ghoul becomes very useful, or having morals blood bound to you. <br /> <br /> I plan on working on the conversion a little bit at a time. Like I said most of it will just be fluff, the crunch should be relatively minor. I may work on clan lore next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T20:24:23-07:00","id":1229284,"title":"","content":"The embrace.<br /> This functions per usual with only a difference in process. It all goes normally until the time comes to have your childe drink. At this point instead of feeding the victim it\u2019s blood the Progeny creates a parasitic blood worm constructed from vitae in his abdomen that is ejected through the mouth. The Progeny\u2019s facial tentacles hold the victim in place while the worm inserts itself into the wound or through the victims mouth. The Progeny at this time hides the now semi lucid childe in a safe dark place, or if abandoned the childe will seek out a suitable hiding place instinctively. Over the course of several days the bloodworm converts the childe into a new Progeny neonate. The exact incubation time varies but is never more than a week. This time the childe is in a state of twilight sedation riddled with nearly indecipherable visions and dreams. <br /> Some think these dreams help prepare one and soften the transition. Others feel it makes the whole process all the more horrifying and confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T22:55:20-07:00","id":1229524,"title":"","content":"After the embrace the Progeny undergo a dramatic metamorphosis. There are no two alike, but certain characteristics travel in families. (This will be fleshed our further in clans and bloodlines) All do share some traits though. <br /> <br /> Each Progeny is humanoid in configuration. Number of fingers, toes, thumbs, and tentacles vary. Rounded or pointed heads are most common with multiple tentacles hanging down concealing a circular lamprey-like mouth lined with teeth. Some specimens have been seen to have squidlike beaks instead of this type of mouth. This gives the head an octopi appearance. <br /> (Rumors speak of high sloping heads resembling certain ancient pharaohs)<br /> Eye and skin colors run the gamut with nigh innumerable possibilities. Random mutations make the number of differing appearances impressive indeed. <br /> Strangely almost all Progeny lack nails, navels, and hair. Exceptions do exist. <br /> <br /> Among the Progeny gender becomes...complicated. After the metamorphosis the Progeny lose all biological traces of gender, but the mental components/drives/desires usually remain. To regain these characters (for a time) they must use blush of life. This temporarily restores human form (more or less) and enables one to recreate if not procreate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T23:14:46-07:00","id":1229527,"title":"","content":"So the infection removes sex but not gender and orientation. <br /> <br /> Anyways, why the discrepancy in using Blush of Life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T23:24:17-07:00","id":1229530,"title":"","content":"Be a bit more specific with discrepancy, there\u2019s a lot going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T23:48:31-07:00","id":1229533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1228178-repurposing-vampires-and-starspawn?p=1229530#post1229530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be a bit more specific with discrepancy, there\u2019s a lot going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was talking about the intra-clan differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T00:06:02-07:00","id":1229537,"title":"","content":"Progeny genetics are....chaotic at best. Prone to mutation and variance. Gives the player a lot of control over what kind of nosfer-thulu there playing. I\u2019m all for creativity. <br /> <br /> As for the blush of life....ventrue are lords among abominations and so exert control not only on others, but there forms. The blush just comes easy to them. As for the Daeva they easily shift form to pursue their vices and ply there trades amongst the sheep.<br /> With regard to nosphoros(nosferatu) well...there humanity seems further left behind than most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T04:15:49-07:00","id":1229561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1228178-repurposing-vampires-and-starspawn?p=1229537#post1229537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Progeny genetics are....chaotic at best. Prone to mutation and variance. Gives the player a lot of control over what kind of nosfer-thulu there playing. I\u2019m all for creativity.<br /> <br /> As for the blush of life....ventrue are lords among abominations and so exert control not only on others, but there forms. The blush just comes easy to them. As for the Daeva they easily shift form to pursue their vices and ply there trades amongst the sheep.<br /> With regard to nosphoros(nosferatu) well...there humanity seems further left behind than most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reasoned, but it seems like the others should get some sort of benefit to compensate. Maybe they are more &quot;stable&quot; since there isn't such a pull between what they were and what they now are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T17:58:37-07:00","id":1229688,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I\u2019ll be honest I\u2019m at a loss to think of a compensating factor. Originally I just planned for all clans to spend a vitae and a willpower, then reasoned the more commanding and social Progeny would be better at it and that Nosphoros, as more monstrous, should be pushed closer to the shadows. I liked the idea of them having to deal more with ghouls and blood-infatuated as go-betweens. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m Always open for suggestions during the creative process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T18:39:45-07:00","id":1229697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1228178-repurposing-vampires-and-starspawn?p=1229688#post1229688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I\u2019ll be honest I\u2019m at a loss to think of a compensating factor. Originally I just planned for all clans to spend a vitae and a willpower, then reasoned the more commanding and social Progeny would be better at it and that Nosphoros, as more monstrous, should be pushed closer to the shadows. I liked the idea of them having to deal more with ghouls and blood-infatuated as go-betweens.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m Always open for suggestions during the creative process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what other Hacks you are making. Just based off core mechanics, maybe you could give them a bonus to resisting Frenzy, since they wear their monster on their skins instead of in their hearts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T20:37:12-07:00","id":1229724,"title":"","content":"If I was to give some sort of offsetting bonus it would more than likely be to the Nosphoros alone. In this whole scenario they seem to be the ones getting the proverbial shaft in retrospect. The restriction on Blush Of Life and there already existing Disquieting Aura. I was going to see about keeping the mechanics as close to the original requiem as I can, that way it would be like learning one system with some changes instead of learning almost two systems.<br /> Honestly, the more I work on this the more I wonder if this should be its own distinct splat. <br /> Drinking blood, fearing the sun, psuedo-psychic abilities, blood sorcery, torpor/hibernation, humanity...it just all seems perfect to me for the adaptation.<br /> Guess my question is before I get hard into the conversion is whether or not this seems like a valid idea, or if im just trampling all over a beloved splat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T01:00:22-07:00","id":1229760,"title":"","content":"Vampire already has a bunch of non-Kindred vampires (often called the Wicked Dead, named for the 1E Night Horrors book they got extensive coverage in), so I say it\u2019s fine. <br /> <br /> But then it does become weird that this thread is in the general forum, not the Vampire one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T02:00:57-07:00","id":1229766,"title":"","content":"Hmm...yes I probably should have put it there in hindsight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar"